# ── KGSM cluster — read by every member on this host ──────────────────────────
# The secret every member of a cluster carries. It is what proves membership: a member trusts any
# caller bearing a service token signed with it. Generate one and copy it to every machine:
#
#   openssl rand -hex 32
#
# Blank means this host is not part of a cluster. That is a state, not a misconfiguration — a
# standalone host leaves it blank and everything cluster-shaped stays dormant.
#
# One file rather than one copy per member, because a machine can run more than one member: a node
# that runs the engine and game servers, and an anchor that provides one capability to the whole
# cluster. Each member's unit loads this BEFORE its own env file, so one could override it
# deliberately — but a member holding a different secret is one the others cannot authenticate, and
# nothing reports that as an error, because "not clustered" and "wrong secret" look identical here.

Cluster__Secret=

# Rotating: put the NEW secret above and the OLD one here, roll every member onto the new one, then
# clear this. Both are accepted while it is set, so a roll needs no downtime.
Cluster__SecretPrevious=
